            <ArticleTitle>Chemical sympathectomy in the relief of persistent sympathetic pain after carpal tunnel release. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>191-3; discussion 194</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although carpal tunnel syndrome (CTS) is a common entrapment neuropathy, reflex sympathetic dystrophy is an extremely rare and devastating complication. In this report, a case of chemical sympathectomy in a patient who had undergone previous three surgical interventions elsewhere for unilateral CTS, with persistent sympathetic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
